    "title": "Isiah Kiner-Falefa connects with Kiner side of family - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Isiah Kiner-Falefa just a few months ago, received a memorable experience during a road trip to New York when the Pirates played the Mets. “For me to not meet anybody on my grandfather’s side. It was kind of felt like something was missing,” said Kiner-Falefa. That ‘missing’ feeling went away as IKF was introduced to his 2nd cousin Scott Kiner, the son of MLB great Ralph Kiner. “To finally meet Scott, it’s all full circle. Like, I’m getting emotional right now, but, like, I mean, this is incredible. This is incredible moment that I never thought would happen,” said Kiner-Falefa. This was the first time IKF was able to meet a family member from the Kiner side of his family and comes during his 2nd season with the Pittsburgh Pirates. On the season, IKF already has more than half the number of total hits he had in 2024, as he sits with 69 total hits in 2025. He also currently has a batting average of .277 with just a few more games before the All-Star Break. Stick with KHON2 Sports for continuing coverage of Athletes from Hawaii in the Pro’s. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KHON2.",
